---
/**
 * /privacy — the Privacy Policy.
 *
 * WRITTEN FROM THE CODE, not from a template. Every practice described below
 * is one this repository actually performs: the quote form fields in
 * quote-actions.ts, the attribution fields and spam checks in
 * quote-submission.ts, the private Blob upload and signed links in
 * api/quote.ts and quote-photo-links.ts, the Resend hand-off in api/quote.ts,
 * and the Google tags in BaseHead.astro. If a practice stops being true in the
 * code, it has to stop being claimed here in the same change.
 *
 * The SMS section is required for A2P 10DLC registration and states, in plain
 * words, that mobile information is never sold or handed to anyone else for
 * their own marketing.
 */
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Load Logic Junk Removal collects, uses, and protects the information you share through this website, including text message consent."
  updated="October 30, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what {BUSINESS.legalName} collects through this website, why we
    collect it, and who it is shared with. It covers this website only.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you give us</h2>
  <p>
    The quote form is the only place this site asks you for anything. When you send a
    request, we collect:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name</li>
    <li>Your phone number</li>
    <li>The ZIP code of the property</li>
    <li>What you need removed</li>
    <li>Photos, if you choose to add them</li>
    <li>Anything you type in the notes box</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Photos and notes are optional. Older versions of our form also accepted an email
    address and a service address, and we still accept those if your browser sends them.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>When you submit the form, our server also records:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The page you submitted from</li>
    <li>
      Campaign tags from the link you arrived on, such as the code on a mailer, so we
      know which advertising brought you to us
    </li>
    <li>
      Your network address, held briefly in memory to limit how many requests one
      connection can send
    </li>
    <li>Two hidden anti-spam values: an unused field and the time the page loaded</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Campaign tags are kept in your browser for the length of your visit so they still
    reach us if you browse before asking for a quote. Closing the tab clears them.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, and Google Ads to understand how people
    find the site and whether our advertising works. These tools set cookies and collect
    usage data under Google's own policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you reach us from a Google ad, Google may show you a temporary forwarding phone
    number in place of ours so the resulting call can be measured. The call still rings
    our business line.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To prepare and send you an estimate</li>
    <li>To contact you about your request, schedule the work, and complete the job</li>
    <li>To confirm the property is in our service area</li>
    <li>To apply a promotional code you arrived with</li>
    <li>To protect the form from automated abuse</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information. We share it only with the services that make this
    site run:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong>, which hosts the site and stores submitted photos</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong>, which delivers your request to our inbox</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong>, for the analytics and advertising described above</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information when the law requires it. Nobody receives your
    information for their own advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Text messages</h2>
  <p>
    The quote form includes an optional checkbox for text messages about your quote,
    scheduling, and service. It is never checked for you, and you can request a quote
    and receive service without ticking it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>
      We will not sell your mobile information. We will not share your mobile information
      with third parties or affiliates for their marketing or promotional purposes.
    </strong>
    Your text message opt-in and the consent record behind it are never shared for
    unrelated marketing, and they are used only to message you about the work you asked
    us about.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can stop messages at any time by replying <strong>STOP</strong>. For help, reply
    <strong>HELP</strong>. Message frequency varies, and message and data rates may
    apply. Our <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a> describe the messaging program
    in full.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you tick the box, we record that you agreed, the wording you agreed to, the time
    our server received it, and that it came from this website's quote form. We keep that
    record so we can show what you consented to.
  </p>

  <h2>Photos</h2>
  <p>
    Photos you send are stored privately. They are not public, and they are not indexed by
    search engines. The link in our notification email opens one photo and stops working
    after 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Quote requests arrive as email in our business inbox and stay there as our record of
    the job. Photos remain in private storage. You can ask us to delete either.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask us what we hold about you, or ask us to delete it</li>
    <li>Reply STOP to any text message to end messages</li>
    <li>Use your browser settings to block or clear cookies</li>
    <li>Call or text us instead of using the form</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is for our customers and is not directed to children under 13. We do not
    knowingly collect information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    {BUSINESS.legalName}<br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phone}`}>{BUSINESS.phoneDisplay}</a><br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
